  "metadata": {
    "title": "Micron Rallies as TD Cowen Lifts Price Target 127% Ahead of Earnings",
    "byline": null,
    "published_at": null,
    "site_name": "finance.yahoo.com",
    "language": null
  },
  "content": {
    "text": "This article first appeared on GuruFocus.\nMicron (MU, Financials) shares jumped after TD Cowen made a much bigger bet on the memory chipmaker ahead of its June 24 earnings report.\nAnalyst Krish Sankar raised his price target to $1,500 from $660 and kept a Buy rating on the stock. The call reflects a simple view: demand for memory used in AI systems is still running ahead of supply, and that could keep prices stronger for longer.\nThat matters for Micron because memory pricing has a major impact on earnings. Sankar now expects Micron to earn about $23 per share in the third quarter, above Wall Street's estimate of about $20. He also sees about $27 per share in the August quarter.\nInvestors will be watching more than just the headline numbers. Updates on pricing, AI server demand and long-term customer agreements could shape expectations for 2027.\nMicron has already rallied sharply this year, so the earnings bar is high. Still, TD Cowen's target raise shows confidence that this memory cycle may have more room to run.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "This article first appeared on GuruFocus.",
      "Micron (MU, Financials) shares jumped after TD Cowen made a much bigger bet on the memory chipmaker ahead of its June 24 earnings report.",
      "Analyst Krish Sankar raised his price target to $1,500 from $660 and kept a Buy rating on the stock. The call reflects a simple view: demand for memory used in AI systems is still running ahead of supply, and that could keep prices stronger for longer.",
      "That matters for Micron because memory pricing has a major impact on earnings. Sankar now expects Micron to earn about $23 per share in the third quarter, above Wall Street's estimate of about $20. He also sees about $27 per share in the August quarter.",
      "Investors will be watching more than just the headline numbers. Updates on pricing, AI server demand and long-term customer agreements could shape expectations for 2027.",
      "Micron has already rallied sharply this year, so the earnings bar is high. Still, TD Cowen's target raise shows confidence that this memory cycle may have more room to run."
    ],
    "html": null
  },
